+# Update every eligible bot's AI once every this many world ticks (1-60,
+# default 1). The world server runs one bot AI tick per world tick, so at a
+# large random-bot population the tick cost scales 1:1 with the pool and the
+# world loop falls behind (seconds per tick at a thousand bots). Raising this
+# staggers the bots that no real player is involved with - no owner/master, no
+# group, not in combat, no network player within ReactDistance - so the cost
+# grows with what the players actually interact with instead of with the pool.
+# Bots a player owns, groups, fights beside, or can see always keep a full
+# update rate, and a staggered bot gets the skipped time handed back on its
+# next run so its own timers stay wall-clock correct. Suggested: 3-5 for a few
+# hundred bots, 5-10 for a thousand.
